auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  The read API of NetMapper: eight GET endpoints behind a bearer token.
  
  Pick the "local" environment and set `token` to the value printed by
  `netmapper token create --name bruno --scope read`. It is a secret variable:
  Bruno keeps its value on this machine and never writes it to the repository.

  Run "List snapshots", "List devices" then "Get device" first: their post-response
  scripts fill `snapshot`, `device`, `interface` and `observation` with the first
  real value from the answer, for the requests that follow. They are runtime
  variables, so the environment file is not modified; the values in "local" are
  only the fallback until those requests have run.

  Contract: specs/005-read-api/contracts/rest.md
}
